# Database Rules

## PostgreSQL — Operational Data
- Every table: id (UUID default gen_random_uuid()), tenant_id (UUID NOT NULL),
  created_at (TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()), updated_at (TIMESTAMPTZ)
- RLS on every table: USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant')::uuid)
- All migrations: zero-downtime expand/contract pattern only
- New NOT NULL columns: always add DEFAULT first, backfill, then add NOT NULL
- CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY — never plain CREATE INDEX on large tables
- Foreign keys on all relationship columns
- Parameterized queries always — never string concatenation

## ClickHouse — Analytics Data
- Engine: ReplicatedMergeTree for production, MergeTree for dev
- Always define ORDER BY (low cardinality first, then high)
- Partition by toYYYYMM(created_at) for time-series tables
- TTL: set data retention policy on all analytics tables
- Batch inserts only: buffer-and-flush, minimum 500 rows or 5 seconds
- Never single-row inserts to ClickHouse
- No JOINs in real-time dashboard queries — pre-aggregate via materialized views

## Migrations
- golang-migrate for Go services
- Prisma Migrate for TypeScript services
- Every migration: up + down scripts
- Never drop columns immediately — mark deprecated, remove in next release
- Test migrations on staging before production always

## Elasticsearch — Ping Search
- Explicit index mappings always — never dynamic mapping in production
- keyword type for exact match fields (tenant_id, status, platform)
- text type for full-text search fields (rejection reason, payload)
- date type for timestamp fields
- Index per tenant for enterprise customers, shared index with tenant_id filter for others